<title>UK: Tesco meat supplier to build plant in Wales.</title>
<headline>Tesco meat supplier to build plant in Wales.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>British meat processer St Merryn Meat Ltd is to build a new 25 million stg meat factory in Merthyr Tydfil in Wales, creating almost 700 new jobs.</p>
<p>St Merryn, which already has seven plants in Devon, Cornwall and Essex, said it was expanding to meet rapidly growing demand from its major customer, supermarket group Tesco Plc</p>
<p>The new plant, which will produce more than 2,000 tonnes of retail meat packs a week, will employ 663 workers, with another 70 jobs being created in supply companies.</p>
<p>The Welsh Development Agency will provide 20 acres of reclaimed land for the project. --London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
